  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math> denote the sum of the first n terms of an arithmetic progression. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>390</mn></math> and the ratio of the tenth and the fifth terms is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>7</mn></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>15</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> is equal to:"
